{"title":"What I’ve been reading","link":"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/923758442/0/marginalrevolution~What-Ive-been-reading.html","date":1756098048000,"content":"<p>David Woodman, <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.amazon.com/First-King-England-%C3%86thelstan-Kingdom/dp/0691249490/ref=sr_1_1?crid=RQAN9JTB6PTX&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.pDM2V3S4CEs9X6eEmR8jiLed_J54hEk7XkqbF-ckI98.pPwhTMUL3hC5kdqYYiphJsvQijlcnvNH8eGmoo4eL3s&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=The+First+King+of+England%3A+Aethelstan+and+the+Birth+of+a+Kingdom&amp;qid=1756069224&amp;sprefix=the+first+king+of+england+aethelstan+and+the+birth+of+a+kingdom%2Caps%2C96&amp;sr=8-1\" target=\"_blank\">The First King of England: Aethelstan and the Birth of a Kingdom</a>.  An excellent work.  One of the best books on early English history, and also one of the best books on how the Dark Ages morphed into early Medieval times.  Usually I find treatments in both areas difficult to follow, but this one produces a coherent and also non-exaggerated narrative.  It also will make you want to visit Northumbria.</p>\r\n<p>Edmund Phelps, <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.amazon.com/Journeys-Economic-Theory-Edmund-Phelps/dp/0231207301/ref=sr_1_1?crid=1UZGOOBS1EOT2&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.Gdd8FUdtp4oSellJVdWSIfcMeEHFNp3SwotgW-O_Wk6-w4warLG2WLWF9q4Kjao4k6P26gQs3Dlil7ekLh80F5bSTGCKLfsH6lyh5ba-Ly0.Li4uDNNS7dH-iI6DmyvUM08A08T3BaIGpVjggylqHKw&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=My+Journeys+in+Economic+Theory&amp;qid=1756069165&amp;sprefix=my+journeys+in+economic+theory%2Caps%2C75&amp;sr=8-1\" target=\"_blank\">My Journeys in Economic Theory</a>.  A fascinating memoir, I had not known he was so obsessed with Rawls and Nagel.  He also loved the tenor Franco Corelli, and was a Birgit Nilsson fan too.  Recommended, for those who like this sort of thing, and who already are familiar with the cast of characters.</p>\r\n<p>Bench Ansfield, <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.amazon.com/Born-Flames-Business-Remaking-American/dp/132409351X/ref=sr_1_1?crid=35MV53F5LIKOC&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.rXM021HmPDlVuK1lHPV2rw.lXdyPHRBLKeyT8oS_QP2M-LODucgaPJBNDatNAoHin4&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=Born+in+Flames%3A+The+Business+of+Arson+and+the+Remaking+of+the+American+City&amp;qid=1756069116&amp;sprefix=born+in+flames+the+business+of+arson+and+the+remaking+of+the+american+city%2Caps%2C66&amp;sr=8-1\" target=\"_blank\">Born in Flames: The Business of Arson and the Remaking of the American City</a>.  Whenever a book demonstrates what people in New Jersey have known for decades, usually it is a good book.</p>\r\n<p>Andrew Sean Greer, <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.amazon.com/Less-Winner-Pulitzer-Prize-Novel/dp/031631613X/ref=sr_1_1?crid=1IAAIFUMMQZPN&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.wieSPJQyjNy5GOFnQKlqv7SW4I_jeJYkj4xpo0Lg9cSrHAmfO0v1kquXQAg3yFAu0eYHfpmGnx7bTTIFJb2ek_7-dqF-v_0tpoxYppWZ1_GkPZMSBS60SOFm8vUvoYjDIDxblRRmZlBffVLwgMb5OcBePKp8wXhDhf8YaruHuYxhWQRJWjV_lMp-rVc3NpGQ29HsIAtJNzWQ1B5qs6I5FQzo8kjN_bNtpUL72gt82JM.TZAcbCtGztxvSeM8TyduBgD2G0CD4FvZCPDF5wXAvBk&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=less+andrew+sean+greer&amp;qid=1756069256&amp;sprefix=andrew+sean+greer%2Caps%2C90&amp;sr=8-1\" target=\"_blank\">Less: A Novel</a>.  I do not like much in contemporary American fiction, but so far I am quite enjoying this one.</p>\r\n<p>Bernd Roeck, <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.amazon.com/World-First-Light-History-Renaissance/dp/069118383X/ref=sr_1_1?crid=139HWTI8ACNL7&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.h5r6y7D_Cl0cOLnGGub-h3pGtmsA0e9LSHI3pdvYvkM.1E7IaiDoiBsGiqQm6fe_XvV5pepNX4nae2deVMEWuhs&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=The+World+at+First+Light%3A+A+New+History+of+the+Renaissance&amp;qid=1756069083&amp;sprefix=the+world+at+first+light+a+new+history+of+the+renaissance%2Caps%2C75&amp;sr=8-1\" target=\"_blank\">The World at First Light: A New History of the Renaissance</a>.  934 pp. of text, covers too many topics in too desultory a fashion?</p>\r\n<p>Pablo A. Pena, <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.amazon.com/Human-Capital-Humans-Accessible-Introduction/dp/022684143X/ref=sr_1_1?crid=36DY11M268IBQ&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.JMwsPMav8ZkwWPusqHJwiA.q8VSw3XwlJWbeoDTkBz-_UFmpz_nXkA9Xx4RFPtwORY&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=Human+Capital+for+Humans%3A+An+Accessible+Introduction+to+the+Economic+Science+of+the+People&amp;qid=1756069031&amp;sprefix=human+capital+for+humans+an+accessible+introduction+to+the+economic+science+of+the+people%2Caps%2C75&amp;sr=8-1\" target=\"_blank\">Human Capital for Humans: An Accessible Introduction to the Economic Science of the People</a>, is a good popular-level introduction to human capital theory.</p>\r\n<p>There is Carl Benedikt Frey, <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.amazon.com/How-Progress-Ends-Technology-Innovation/dp/0691233071/ref=sr_1_1?crid=K36AECJ1K64C&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.fyPnQQqXumNYRqlAiUWOeg.-NThroNHtht6ggaHXuJb_uL6V3MiS8mSKYub5_bym9s&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=How+Progress+Ends%3A+Technology%2C+Innovation%2C+and+the+Fate+of+Nations&amp;qid=1756068997&amp;sprefix=how+progress+ends+technology%2C+innovation%2C+and+the+fate+of+nations%2Caps%2C77&amp;sr=8-1\" target=\"_blank\">How Progress Ends: Technology, Innovation, and the Fate of Nations</a>.</p>\r\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/08/what-ive-been-reading-275.html\">What I’ve been reading</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com\">Marginal REVOLUTION</a>.</p>\r\n<img height=\"1\" width=\"1\" src=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/i/923758442/0/marginalrevolution\" />\r\n<div><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/28/923758442/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.